# Dataset — 10.6GB archive plus its extracted/cleaned output. Documented as a download step in
# README.md instead (Kaggle aliabdelmenam/rdd-2022). Also covers data.yaml/data_fast.yaml —
# prepare_dataset.py writes these with a machine-specific absolute path baked in (that's exactly
# what caused the stale-data bug this project already hit once — see ASBcode.md), so they should
# never be committed, only regenerated locally.
data/RDD2022/archive.zip
data/RDD2022/download.log
data/RDD2022/extracted/
data/RDD2022/clean/
data/RDD2022/data.yaml
data/RDD2022/data_fast.yaml

# Model weights — all downloaded or trained locally, not authored. Re-fetch/re-train per
# README.md rather than committing binaries.
weights/**/*.pt
weights/**/*.pth
weights/**/*.weights
weights/**/*.ckpt
weights/nanodet_m/_load_logs/

# Vendored NanoDet source (see plugins/nanodet_m.py for why it's a clone, not a pip install) —
# re-clone per README.md rather than committing someone else's repo (with its own .git) into ours.
third_party/nanodet/

# Training run artifacts (checkpoints-in-progress, sample batch images, per-epoch logs) —
# regenerable by re-running the relevant training script.
training/runs/

# NanoDet configs generated fresh at runtime by train_nanodet_m.py / test_nanodet_m.py (absolute
# paths baked in, same reasoning as data.yaml above) — not meant to be hand-edited or committed.
training/nanodet_m_rdd2022.generated.yml
training/nanodet_m_rdd2022_test.generated.yml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

runs/